<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>IEEE Paper Template</title>
<style>
  body {
    font-family: "Times New Roman", serif;
    background-color: whitesmoke;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .paper {
    background-color: white;
    max-width: 850px;
    margin: 50px 50px 100px 250px;
    padding: 40px;
    box-shadow: 1px 1px 8px gray;
  }

  /* Title area */
  .title {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .authors {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
  }

  .affiliation {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-style: italic;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    color: dimgray;
  }

  /* Abstract and Keywords (full width, before columns) */
  .abstract {
    font-size: 13px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .abstract b {
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* Two column layout for the body */
  .content {
    column-count: 2;
    column-gap: 25px;
    font-size: 13px;
    text-align: justify;
  }

  .content h2 {
    font-size: 14px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border-bottom: 1px solid black;
    padding-bottom: 3px;
  }

  .content p {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .references {
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .references p {
    margin: 4px 0;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="paper">

    <!-- Title -->
    <div class="title">Title of Your IEEE Research Paper Goes Here</div>

    <!-- Authors -->
    <div class="authors">First Author, Second Author, Third Author</div>
    <div class="affiliation">Department of Computer Science, Air University, Islamabad, Pakistan</div>

    <!-- Abstract -->
    <div class="abstract">
      <b>Abstract—</b> This is a short summary of your research paper. It explains the problem,
      your method, and the main result in just a few sentences. Keep it brief and simple.
      <br><br>
      <b><i>Keywords—</i></b> HTML, CSS, IEEE format, template, web design
    </div>

    <!-- Two Column Body -->
    <div class="content">

      <h2>I. Introduction</h2>
      <p>
        This section introduces the topic of your paper. Explain the background,
        why the problem is important, and what your paper will cover.
      </p>

      <h2>II. Related Work</h2>
      <p>
        This section discusses previous research done by others on this topic
        and how your work is different or improves upon it.
      </p>

      <h2>III. Methodology</h2>
      <p>
        Explain the method, tools, or approach used to carry out your research
        or build your project.
      </p>

      <h2>IV. Results</h2>
      <p>
        Present the outcome of your work here. You can describe tables, graphs,
        or findings from your experiment.
      </p>

      <h2>V. Conclusion</h2>
      <p>
        Summarize what was achieved in the paper and suggest future improvements
        or next steps.
      </p>

      <h2>References</h2>
      <div class="references">
        <p>[1] Author Name, "Title of the paper," Journal Name, vol. 1, no. 1, pp. 1-5, 2024.</p>
        <p>[2] Author Name, "Title of the paper," Conference Name, pp. 10-15, 2023.</p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>

</body>
</html>
